bbots CHANGELOG
===============

BETA 3.0 (twitch) - October 2026
--------------------------------
The Twitch port. Same bot, same module system, new network.

Connection
  * Connects to Twitch chat over TLS with ncat. ntcpclient is retired.
  * Logs in with a token from the bot's own Twitch application.
    bin/gettoken.sh gets it once and startbot.sh renews it before
    every connection.
  * Reconnects on a dropped connection, when Twitch asks it to, and
    when nothing has been heard from Twitch for ten minutes.
  * Refuses to start a second copy of itself.

People
  * Three tiers: owner (.omod), admin (.amod), anyone (.umod).
    Admins are a channel's broadcaster, its moderators and the names
    on its admin list. New command: admin list | add | rm.
  * Owners are whoever is on the owner list. Twitch logins cannot be
    borrowed the way IRC nicks could.
  * Tier changes: o2u and u2o as before, plus o2a, a2o, u2a, a2u.

Channels
  * The bot can be in many channels. join and part manage the list,
    which is kept in files/lists/channels.lst and rejoined on start.
  * It talks more slowly where it is not a moderator, as Twitch requires.

Modules
  * Default trigger is ! (was .).
  * load refuses a module that has a syntax error.
  * Private messages are gone on Twitch. What used to be a private
    message is said in the channel.
  * pig2: every command under "pig", one game per channel, games
    survive a restart, 2007 win records carried over.
  * translate: uses the MyMemory service.
  * fortune: one line, in the channel.
  * rolldice: any of the three numbers may be left out.
  * additem: owner only, and it will not write to the owner or
    channel lists.
  * trig: "!trig" works now. In 2007 it compared five characters to
    six and never matched.
  * uptime: answers to "botuptime".
  * Modules check their input before using it.
  * Not carried over: irccommands, beep, beep_toggle, cal.

Tools
  * bin/bbots-ctl: a console that passes commands to the running bot
    without anything appearing in chat.
  * runme.sh: starts the bot in the background, and gained the
    console and Twitch login options.

